  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 205 AM EDT Mon May 11 2026\n\n- Frost/Freeze conditions again tonight\n\nExpect one more cold night as a Canadian surface high remains in \nplace tonight with clear skies and light winds. Frost/freeze \nconditions could impact much of the forecast area. The sfc high \nis moving east and clouds may arrive from the west late in the \nnight but temperatures could still fall below freezing in the \ncold spots where winds stay decoupled.\n\n- Rain chances Tuesday and Late Week\n\nA clipper low moving in the fast northwest flow arrives on Tuesday\nwith the first widespread rain this month. QPF expected to be\naround two tenths of an inch with some isolated half inch amounts\npossible with scattered convection Tuesday evening.\n\nFlow goes more zonal late week and deeper moisture streams up from\nthe Gulf ahead of a shortwave trough that arrives Friday or\nSaturday with showers and scattered convection.",
